WEBVTT

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:13.753
AI agents take on routine work: checking that the store opened on time, chasing a supplier order, sorting guest feedback. In this video, you’ll see your agents, how they run, and how everything they do is logged.

00:00:14.833 --> 00:00:25.287
Open Agents. Worklynq agents look things up and, when you allow it, create and update tickets and docs. Each one works as the person who runs it, never with more access.

00:00:25.733 --> 00:00:35.909
Run one yourself, on a schedule, or when a ticket reaches a stage, and choose whether it asks before making changes. Create agent starts a new one from a description.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:42.255
Connected agents lists your team’s own Claude, ChatGPT or Cursor, connected to Worklynq.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:50.188
And once GitHub is connected, a Coding agents tab hands a ticket to Claude or Cursor, and gets a pull request back.

00:00:51.167 --> 00:01:01.108
And Activity logs everything any agent did: what it read, what it changed, whether it worked, and who it acted for. Filter by agent, or show changes only.

